{"id": "EUVD-2026-5844", "enisaUuid": "feb0db4d-e4f4-3cfa-a608-c30823a0b6fe", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nceph: fix oops due to invalid pointer for kfree() in parse_longname()\n\nThis fixes a kernel oops when reading ceph snapshot directories (.snap),\nfor example by simply running `ls /mnt/my_ceph/.snap`.\n\nThe variable str is guarded by __free(kfree), but advanced by one for\nskipping the initial '_' in snapshot names. Thus, kfree() is called\nwith an invalid pointer.  This patch removes the need for advancing the\npointer so kfree() is called with correct memory pointer.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1. Create snapshots on a cephfs volume (I've 63 snaps in my testcase)\n\n2. Add cephfs mount to fstab\n$ echo \"samba-fileserver@.files=/volumes/datapool/stuff/3461082b-ecc9-4e82-8549-3fd2590d3fb6      /mnt/test/stuff   ceph     acl,noatime,_netdev    0       0\" >> /etc/fstab\n\n3. Reboot the system\n$ systemctl reboot\n\n4. Check if it's really mounted\n$ mount | grep stuff\n\n5. List snapshots (expected 63 snapshots on my system)\n$ ls /mnt/test/stuff/.snap\n\nNow ls hangs forever and the kernel log shows the oops.", "datePublished": "2026-02-14T16:27:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-14T11:58:12", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c9a129c82ddf82a50b4f8960d2609714ca2dbd26", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8c9af7339de419819cfc641d551675d38ff99abf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e258ed369c9e04caa7d2fd49785d753ae4034cb6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bc8dedae022ce3058659c3addef3ec4b41d15e00"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3mg9-9f72-h562", "CVE-2026-23201"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "110b7126-7b00-3456-ac2a-cb84000b57b1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.16.1 <6.17"}, {"id": "1b924c6d-f630-3a0f-b7b9-6e1fc1791c4a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "493479af8af3ab907f49e99323777d498a4fbd2b"}, {"id": "28a7002f-33db-3900-90b6-2dead3845e88", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.10"}, {"id": "37dd1463-e513-3b07-808c-894354a19ee0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.17"}, {"id": "3b680327-8c54-322d-b70b-4f8725085b34", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "101841c38346f4ca41dc1802c867da990ffb32eb <e258ed369c9e04caa7d2fd49785d753ae4034cb6"}, {"id": "44403cb0-e8dd-39f5-9664-bdaf286b9b85", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "4e007922-60c8-3617-b4f5-ab699405ff39", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3145b2b11492d61c512bbc59660bb823bc757f48"}, {"id": "523c11d3-19f7-3eae-bf27-97bf15c9c6e8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.70"}, {"id": "87158096-66f8-3139-bfcf-02909a685485", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "101841c38346f4ca41dc1802c867da990ffb32eb <bc8dedae022ce3058659c3addef3ec4b41d15e00"}, {"id": "a6940e95-4412-339a-a4f9-47abc7e2d437", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb80f7618832d26f7e395f52f82b1dac76223e5f <8c9af7339de419819cfc641d551675d38ff99abf"}, {"id": "be6254b6-810e-3d69-9d0f-ff0730fff0c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.42 <6.12.70"}, {"id": "d5d1decf-0158-3729-9c31-6951dcd92630", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19"}, {"id": "efb37b11-0dbf-329b-9e79-9577d9ae38e4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15.10 <6.16"}, {"id": "f5b46704-6372-3629-8266-506d613552da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4b9aee707c4580511983a0998547f3b28514e6a6 <c9a129c